{"files": [{"id": 31003663, "name": "jp1c06468_si_001.pdf", "size": 200670, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/31003663", "supplied_md5": "b5b949b93d21b2c78822840db8764bf9", "computed_md5": "b5b949b93d21b2c78822840db8764bf9", "mimetype": "application/pdf"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 1427122, "full_name": "Jose\u0301 Zu\u0301n\u0303iga", "first_name": "Jose\u0301", "last_name": "Zu\u0301n\u0303iga", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1427134, "full_name": "Adolfo Bastida", "first_name": "Adolfo", "last_name": "Bastida", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1427131, "full_name": "Alberto Requena", "first_name": "Alberto", "last_name": "Requena", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1467967, "full_name": "Javier Cerezo", "first_name": "Javier", "last_name": "Cerezo", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://acs.figshare.com/articles/journal_contribution/_i_Ab_Initio_i_Partition_Functions_and_Thermodynamic_Quantities_for_the_Molecular_Hydrogen_Isotopologues/16752532", "download_disabled": false, "description": "In this work, we\ncalculate the partition functions and thermodynamic\nquantities of molecular hydrogen isotopologues using the rovibrational\nenergy levels provided by the highly accurate <i>ab initio</i> adiabatic potential energy functions recently determined by Pachucki\nand Komasa (Pachucki, K.; Komasa, J. <i>J. Chem. Phys.</i> <b>2014</b>, <i>141</i>, 224103). The partition\nfunctions are calculated by including all bound energy levels of the\nisotopologues, up to their dissociation limits, plus the quasi-bound\nlevels lying below the centrifugal potential barriers. For the homonuclear\nisotopologues, H<sub>2</sub>, D<sub>2</sub>, and T<sub>2</sub>, we\nalso determine the partition functions and thermodynamic quantities\nof the normal mixtures using the statistical treatment recently proposed\nby Colonna et al. (Colonna, G.; D\u2019Angola, A.; Capitelli, M. <i>Int. J. Hydrogen Energy</i> <b>2012</b>, <i>37</i>, 9656) based on the definition of the partition function of the\nmixture, which avoids inconsistencies in the values of the thermodynamic\nquantities depending directly on the internal partition function,\nin the high-temperature limit.", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 200670, "created_date": "2021-10-06T16:05:25Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-02T15:11:22Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 10, "name": "CC BY-NC 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"}, "tags": ["normal mixtures using", "centrifugal potential barriers", "bound levels lying", "bound energy levels", "hydrogen energy </", "ab initio </", ">, 224103 ).", "molecular hydrogen isotopologues", "colonna et al", "internal partition function", "k .; komasa", "partition function", ">, 9656", "37 </", "141 </", "partition functions", "g .;", ".; capitelli", "\u2019 angola", "thermodynamic quantities", "temperature limit", "phys .</", "homonuclear isotopologues", "highly accurate", "dissociation limits", "avoids inconsistencies", "also determine"], "keywords": ["normal mixtures using", "centrifugal potential barriers", "bound levels lying", "bound energy levels", "hydrogen energy </", "ab initio </", ">, 224103 ).", "molecular hydrogen isotopologues", "colonna et al", "internal partition function", "k .; komasa", "partition function", ">, 9656", "37 </", "141 </", "partition functions", "g .;", ".; capitelli", "\u2019 angola", "thermodynamic quantities", "temperature limit", "phys .</", "homonuclear isotopologues", "highly accurate", "dissociation limits", "avoids inconsistencies", "also determine"], "categories": [{"id": 915, "title": "Physical Sciences not elsewhere classified", "parent_